api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/deployments","created_at":"2018-11-27T03:35:03Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T09:08:20Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-10T20:45:00Z","git_url":"git://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy","homepage":"https://www.sqlalchemy.org","size":99269,"stargazers_count":11252,"watchers_count":11252,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1606,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":205,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["python","sql","sqlalchemy"],"visibility":"public","forks":1606,"open_issues":205,"watchers":11252,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\n`filter` with following relationship does work correctly, but `filter_by` does not work.\r\nAlmost the same logic was working correctly with SQLAlchemy 1.3.24.\r\n\r\nIMO, #7239 is related.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import ForeignKey\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Integer\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import String\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import relationship\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Session\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass GrandParent(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'grand_parents'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n    children = relationship('Parent')\r\n    grand_children = relationship('Child', secondary='parents', lazy='dynamic', viewonly=True)\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Parent(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'parents'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    grand_parent_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey('grand_parents.id'), nullable=False)\r\n\r\n    children = relationship('Child')\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Child(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'children'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    sex = Column(String)\r\n    parent_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey('parents.id'), nullable=False)\r\n\r\n    __mapper_args__ = {\r\n        'polymorphic_on': sex,\r\n        'polymorphic_identity': 'unknown',\r\n        'with_polymorphic': '*'\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Boy(Child):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'boys'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey('children.id'), primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n    __mapper_args__ = {\r\n        'polymorphic_identity': 'male',\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Girl(Child):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'girls'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey('children.id'), primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n    __mapper_args__ = {\r\n        'polymorphic_identity': 'female',\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\nengine = create_engine('sqlite://', echo=True, future=True)\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(engine)\r\n\r\nwith Session(engine) as session:\r\n    grand_parent = GrandParent()\r\n    parent = Parent()\r\n    child = Boy()\r\n\r\n    grand_parent.children.append(parent)\r\n    parent.children.append(child)\r\n\r\n    session.add(grand_parent)\r\n    session.commit()\r\n\r\n\r\nwith Session(engine) as session:\r\n    grand_parent = session.query(GrandParent).get(1)\r\n\r\n    # Success\r\n    child = grand_parent.grand_children.filter(Child.id == 1).first()\r\n\r\n    # Failed\r\n    child = grand_parent.grand_children.filter_by(id=1).first()\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/sql/base.py\", line 1222, in __getattr__\r\n    return self._index[key]\r\nKeyError: 'id'\r\n\r\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\r\n\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/sql/base.py\", line 1693, in _entity_namespace_key\r\n    return getattr(ns, key)\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/sql/base.py\", line 1224, in __getattr__\r\n    util.raise_(AttributeError(key), replace_context=err)\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/util/compat.py\", line 207, in raise_\r\n    raise exception\r\nAttributeError: id\r\n\r\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\r\n\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"reproduce.py\", line 82, in <module>\r\n    child = grand_parent.grand_children.filter_by(id=1).first()\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/orm/query.py\", line 1795, in filter_by\r\n    for key, value in kwargs.items()\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/orm/query.py\", line 1795, in <listcomp>\r\n    for key, value in kwargs.items()\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/sql/base.py\", line 1700, in _entity_namespace_key\r\n    replace_context=err,\r\n  File \"/home/centos/.pyenv/versions/sqlalchemy-issue/lib/python3.